# B198 — rogueone's node-exporter, SYSTEMD COLLECTOR ONLY. Installed as /etc/default/prometheus-node-exporter
# (the Ubuntu package's EnvironmentFile; its unit runs `prometheus-node-exporter $ARGS`).
#
# WHY ONLY SYSTEMD: the exporter exists so the nightly placement-coverage CronJob (scripts/placement_check.py --live)
# can read which services and timers run on rogueone. The default collectors would add node_filesystem_* / memory
# series, and k8s/monitoring/node-disk-alerts.yaml matches node_filesystem_* with no job filter — a laptop would then be
# judged by mother's disk thresholds. `unit-include` keeps services + timers only (the check ignores other types).
# Scraped by Prometheus as job `systemd-rogueone` (k8s/monitoring/kube-prometheus-stack-values.yaml).
#
# Install (package without recommends — the "collectors" recommend adds its own timers):
#   sudo apt install -y --no-install-recommends prometheus-node-exporter
#   sudo install -m 644 nodes/rogueone/systemd/prometheus-node-exporter.default /etc/default/prometheus-node-exporter
#   sudo systemctl restart prometheus-node-exporter
# Verify: curl -s localhost:9100/metrics | grep -c '^node_systemd_unit_state'
ARGS="--collector.disable-defaults --collector.systemd --collector.systemd.unit-include=.+[.](service|timer) --web.listen-address=:9100"
